{{!-- What is the character's but not under their direct possession: a sword dropped when Fatigue
      came in, a crest left at an inn, and every mule and cart, which are never direct possession
      at all — you may hold the rein, but if you run, whether the beast comes is the Warden's to
      say. Written down so it is not forgotten; weighing nothing, because nothing you are not
      holding can cost you a slot.

      This is the only zone whose "add" control makes something the character does not have to
      hand. A thing remembered after the fact cannot be created on the ten and then set aside — a
      full inventory has no room to hold it for that one instant.

      It draws the same list as Petty. The two hold the same kind of row and differ only in what
      put it there, so they are one template and the eye finds every control in the same place on
      both. --}}
<section class="tab {{tabs.belongings.cssClass}}" data-group="primary" data-tab="belongings">
    <div class="cairn-zone-head">
        <h4 class="cairn-zone">{{localize 'CAIRN.Belongings'}}</h4>
        {{#if editable}}
        <a class="cairn-zone-add" data-action="belongingCreate">
            <i class="fas fa-plus" inert></i><span>{{localize 'CAIRN.Add'}}</span>
        </a>
        {{/if}}
    </div>
    <div class="cairn-zone-rule" data-ink="hline" data-ink-seed="zone-belongings" data-ink-w="1" data-ink-a="0.34"></div>
    {{> "systems/cairn2e/templates/parts/plain-list.hbs" rows=inventory.belongings seed="belonging"
        empty=(localize 'CAIRN.NoBelongings')}}
</section>
